   $ K^1 arrow.r^u K^2 $ <p3sw:support-two-term-model>]
  for $G$. On $M^compose$ its fiber map is surjective. Thus $u^(*) : \( K^2 \)^(*) arrow.r \( K^1 \)^(*)$ is generically injective. The variety $M$ is integral, and the source of $u^(*)$ is locally free; its generically zero kernel must therefore be zero. Dualizing (4.43) and shifting as in (4.37) leaves its sole cohomology in degree zero, with resolution
  #[#set math.equation(numbering: n => "(4.44)")
