=== 4.4 The coherent translation action and the quotient <the-coherent-translation-action-and-the-quotient>

For the group action, enumerate the source cosets in (4.9) by $G_2$ and $G_1$, respectively. Translation on a closed invariant subscheme gives its ideal the canonical translation linearization, so $I = I_Sigma times.square I_A$ has a genuine $G_1 times G_2$-linearization for the source translations. The word “coherent” in the next statement includes the composition isomorphisms, not only one isomorphism for each group element.

